WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.262
The final SELECT exposes the results of the pipeline.

00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:07.957
Phone candidates are only kept when they satisfy the ten-digit teaching rule.

00:00:07.957 --> 00:00:12.907
Unsupported dates remain NULL. Duplicate rank remains visible.

00:00:12.907 --> 00:00:18.557
The row status flags records that still contain important unresolved problems.

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:24.822
This is what transparent cleaning looks like: useful output plus visible uncertainty.

00:00:24.822 --> 00:00:31.327
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:31.327 --> 00:00:36.612
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:44.037
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:49.537
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.537 --> 00:00:55.440
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
